# Banter in Dawn's Gate and the Howlers Pass (story/banter.gd plays this file only where a place's region is dawns_gate): one exchange between two or three companions about what is in
# front of them in one place, gated on that place (`at:`) and on the story's state so a remark never runs ahead of the chapter. Played now and then on entering
# an area, once each; an exchange nobody present can speak comes out empty and is skipped.
# Drafted by Gemini (docs/plans/gemini_companions/), edited; every edit is listed in the README there. Lines are unvoiced until the voice lane reads them.


~ dawns_gate_01_delphine_silas
if name:delphine_ravelle and name:silas_vane and at:dawns_gate and not flag.renathyr_slain
interject name:delphine_ravelle: Soot on the cobbles and the same red rag nailed to every door, Silas. Whoever dressed this house had a heavy hand with the red paint.
interject name:silas_vane: Look up the hill at those red windows, because the management is clearly keeping an eye on the table. Even the smelter smoke tastes like copper stakes.
interject name:delphine_ravelle: My Fool is pulling faces at that heap of slag, and he does not even have a nose to wrinkle. Mind the seams, the ash gets into everything.
interject name:silas_vane: Ash I can brush off my ribs, Delphine, it is the timbered mine adit that bothers me. When a town boards up its only living, the game is already rigged.
endif
-> END

~ dg_briar_02_tobin_rook
if name:tobin_hayward and name:rook_coldwake and at:dg_briar and not flag.renathyr_slain
interject name:tobin_hayward: Keep me three paces back from that hearth, Rook, the fire is drawing too fierce for dry burlap. At least Kristoff Gruber keeps his onions dry and his rafters clean of rot.
interject name:rook_coldwake: Low beams are a hazard for a tall shield, Tobin, though the masonry round the chimney is sound enough. Quiet sort of shift when nobody in the taproom sings.
interject name:tobin_hayward: That pot on the hob was a goat once, before someone boiled the sins right out of it. Still, the mice in my lapels are twitching for a crust.
interject name:rook_coldwake: Let them have my share of the broth, then, and remind me to sigh before we go up the stair. A watchman looks unruly if he sits by a good fire without breathing.
interject name:tobin_hayward: You breathe when you please, Rook, just do not let that brass knocker on your shield clack while I am shaking the beetles out of my head.
endif
-> END

~ dg_briar_cellar_03_lucan_cordelia
if name:lucan_houndstooth and name:cordelia_skein and at:dg_briar and not flag.renathyr_slain
interject name:lucan_houndstooth: Hush now, Cordelia, Barnaby has his nose to the flagstones by the third rack. He never points at casks of black beer unless the stonework itself is dishonest.
interject name:cordelia_skein: Your spectral Pomeranian has an admirable eye for masonry. The mortar behind those barrels is decades fresher than the cellar around it, and the air leaks right through.
interject name:lucan_houndstooth: Let me take a brief sniff by the barley sacks, if you please. Damp lime, bruised hops, and the distinct spoor of someone bricks could not keep out.
interject name:cordelia_skein: My six eyes just clicked at the draught coming through that seam, Lucan. Stand back while we pry it open, my pulse charts love a surprise.
interject name:lucan_houndstooth: Good heavens, I only hope whatever waits behind the false wall has better posture than the last specimen we cornered in the dark.
endif
-> END

~ dg_briar_upper_04_silas_lucan
if name:silas_vane and name:lucan_houndstooth and at:dg_briar and not flag.renathyr_slain
interject name:silas_vane: Four narrow beds under the eaves and I do not even sleep, Lucan, so you can have my bolster for Barnaby. Just keep the window shut against that red glare on the hill.
interject name:lucan_houndstooth: You are most gracious, Silas, though Barnaby prefers to curl beneath my coat on the floor hook. One clap of mountain thunder and he forgets he is a harbinger of dread.
interject name:silas_vane: Better a dog that hides under a coat than a shadow that lags half a step behind your boots. Mine has been staring at that traveller's chest since we came up.
interject name:lucan_houndstooth: Do not let the red light rattle your cards, friend. If you must spend four hours in revelry tonight, perhaps we might play a quiet hand on the blanket.
interject name:silas_vane: You are on, Lucan, provided the hound does not yip every time I palm an ace off the bottom.
endif
-> END

~ mon_pass_05_cordelia_silas
if name:cordelia_skein and name:silas_vane and at:mon_pass and not flag.renathyr_slain
interject name:cordelia_skein: Read the signpost, Silas, the Crimson Rose receives all, which sounds delightfully thorough. With those bats streaming from the belfry, the pathology up here must be thriving.
interject name:silas_vane: When a house puts out a welcome sign on a dead mountain, friend, check the fine print before you step through the gate. Even the wind through my ribs tastes like cold iron.
interject name:cordelia_skein: Mind your footing on the loose slate, I cannot calibrate my vials if I am catching you on every bend. Look how the red windows light the stone like an artery.
interject name:silas_vane: My censer is swinging three inches wider than it should, Cordelia, and the dead trees are leaning in to watch the deal. House always wins, unless you burn the house.
interject name:cordelia_skein: Then let us climb to the watch at the gate and see what sort of humours keep those lamps burning all night.
endif
-> END

~ dawns_gate_06_delphine_lucan
if name:delphine_ravelle and name:lucan_houndstooth and at:dawns_gate and flag.renathyr_slain
interject name:delphine_ravelle: Renathyr is dead, Lucan, and yet the red windows up there are still staring down like cheap stage lights. At least the square has stopped holding its breath.
interject name:lucan_houndstooth: The air by the village well is cleaner, if you please, more river water and less old blood in the soot. Even Barnaby is trotting past the bell post with his tail up.
interject name:delphine_ravelle: My Fool had three puns ready for the smelter and he dropped every one of them on the hill path. When a town goes this quiet after the curtain falls, it gives my stitching a chill.
interject name:lucan_houndstooth: They have lived under that black tower a very long time, Delphine. Give them an evening to learn that the dark on the peak no longer has teeth.
endif
-> END

~ mon_pass_07_rook_silas
if name:rook_coldwake and name:silas_vane and at:mon_pass and flag.renathyr_slain
interject name:rook_coldwake: Loose slate is worse coming down than going up, Silas, and the grade on these bends is five degrees past regulation. Mind the turf by that cold fire ring.
interject name:silas_vane: Scratch one more chalk tally inside my ribs for Renathyr, Rook, and call the tab settled. Walking away from the table with all our bones is the best hand we will get.
interject name:rook_coldwake: Look at the pilgrims' cairn by the dead tree, every stone stacked neat by folk who marched up to that gate. I should take a chalk rubbing for the ledger before we leave the foot of the climb.
interject name:silas_vane: Leave the stones to the bats in the belfry, the living down the hill have had enough of ledgers. Come on, I will remind you to breathe when we hit the river road.
interject name:rook_coldwake: Fair enough, Silas. Settle down now, and keep your shadow on the path where I can see it.
endif
-> END
